.TH IMPROV-SAVE-VIEW 1 "" "improv" "Improv Manual"
.SH NAME
improv\-save\-view \- Save a named view of a measure, as the GUI does
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBimprov save\-view\fR [OPTIONS] <db> <view\-id> <name> <measure>
.SH DESCRIPTION
Save a named view of a measure, as the GUI does.
.PP
\-\-rows and \-\-cols stack category names outer to inner; each defaults to the next unused category of the measure. The other categories are pages, pinned to their first item. A view with the same id is replaced.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-rows\fR \fI<Cat,...>\fR
The row categories, comma\-separated, outer first
.TP
\fB\-\-cols\fR \fI<Cat,...>\fR
The column categories, comma\-separated, outer first
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
.TP
<\fIdb\fR>
The model store: a file, or postgres://USER@HOST/DB?model=NAME
.TP
<\fIview\-id\fR>
The view\*(Aqs numeric id
.TP
<\fIname\fR>
The view\*(Aqs name
.TP
<\fImeasure\fR>
The measure, by id or name
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR improv (1).
